--
N5008 [class.compare.default]/1-2: a defaulted comparison operator may be a
FRIEND of the class taking two `const C &' parameters; it is defined as the
memberwise comparison ([class.eq]/2) exactly like the defaulted member form
`bool operator==(const C &) const = default'.  The friend form failed with
"symbol '' is unknown" at the declaration and the translation unit was
rejected.  Round-163 diagnosis: not the friend form -- the synthesized
memberwise comparison ([class.compare.default]/6: base classes and
non-static data MEMBERS) also compared the anonymous padding component the
layout inserts between `char *ptr' and `errc ec'; the member form failed
the same way for any padded class (the original `point' has none).  Fixed
in round 163 (padding skipped for defaulted ==, != and <=>).  This is libc++'s std::to_chars_result
(`friend bool operator==(const to_chars_result &, const to_chars_result &) =
default'), whose operator== body is dropped in every libc++ C++20 test
(audit residue item 3, round 162).
